    <item>
      <title>The Fading Light of Wisdom</title>
      <description>Today&apos;s story will change how you see everything... In the dense forest of Dvaita, King Janaka sat on his throne, surrounded by his advisors. He had been a just ruler, loved by all, but as the years passed, his energy began to wane. He spent his days in idle conversations, his nights in lavish feasts. His armies grew weak, his economy faltered. The wise sage, Ashtavakra, arrived at the palace, his eyes burning with a fire that seemed to pierce through the shadows. &apos;Your Highness,&apos; he said, &apos;you are a shadow of your former self. Your sloth has consumed you, and with it, your kingdom.&apos; Janaka looked up, his eyes clouded with a mixture of sorrow and regret. &apos;I fear I have lost my way,&apos; he said. Ashtavakra placed his hand on Janaka&apos;s shoulder. &apos;The path to wisdom is not an easy one,&apos; he said. &apos;But it is not too late to turn back. Remember the words of the great king, &apos;A tree that does not yield fruit in its season is cut down.&apos; Janaka&apos;s eyes widened as the truth hit him. He had been cutting down his own kingdom, one decision at a time. With a newfound sense of purpose, he rose from his throne and vowed to reclaim his kingdom, to reignite the fire that once burned within him. This is Sloth — the sin of idleness that can consume even the greatest of empires. Today, we struggle with procrastination, with putting off until tomorrow what we can do today. Ask yourself, what is holding you back from achieving your dreams?</description>
      <pubDate>Wed, 15 Apr 2026 09:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
